synopsis:       Typeclasses for type conversion mappings
description:    This package provides the typeclasses 'From' and 'TryFrom'.
                .
                The 'From.From' typeclass provides @'From.from' :: a -> b@. It is an
                interface a pair of types that can be converted from one to another.
                .
                The 'From.TryFrom' typeclass provides @'From.tryFrom' :: a -> 'Prelude.Maybe'
                b@. It is an interface for a pair of types that can be converted from one to
                another, safely handling the possibility of a failure.
                .
                Default 'From.From' instances are provided for some integral types in base,
                using 'Prelude.fromIntegral'.
                .
                This is the core package. This package itself is not spectacularly useful.
                One example of immediate usefulness would be the @from-string@ package.
